# Blow a Horn of Goodness and read the protective white-floor field's radius
# directly from the player-facing map. Read the horizontal row through the `@`
# in @dump:goodness-field: the white GLYPH_FLOOR2 patch reaches six squares
# from the player, which is 60 feet at 10 feet per square.
#
# ON A BUILD WITHOUT THE FIX the same dump shows radius 2: the white-floor
# field reaches only two squares (20 feet) from `@`. The separate fear globe's
# lval 6 is not measured here; this oracle reads the field painted by NewField.
#
# Auto-Identify Items makes the acquired horn's true name available to the
# Activate menu. Item Acquisition's Horns category is RIGHT*28, following the
# established horn-madness and horn-panic oracles. The horn is given plus 1;
# its plus does not control the explicitly coded field radius. Run with seed 1.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE                   # Auto-Identify Items
ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*28                # Horns
@until "Horn of Goodness" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
1                       # known plus; the field radius is independent of plus
ENTER
a                       # empty Ready Hand slot
SPACE                   # complete assignment; clear the In-the-Air slot
@dump:horn-carried
ESC

A                       # Activate an Item (shifted command)
@until "Which magic item do you wish to activate?" a
a                       # choose [a] Horn of Goodness
@dump:goodness-field

@quit
